   "mechanisms_outside_ir": [],
   "notes": "The headline model is the Chinese RoFormer (WoBERT with its absolute position embedding replaced by RoPE). It is the model used for the long-text benchmark named in the abstract and the Huggingface release. Other settings are not described: the MT encoder-decoder on Transformer-base, the English BERT (bert-base-uncased) replacement, and Performer+RoPE on enwik8 with 12 layers, 768 dimensions and 12 heads. The paper states only the positional mechanism. RoPE uses interleaved adjacent pairs, theta base 10000, and rotates all dimensions. All size fields are left not_stated, as are norm, FFN and activation, biases and the MLM head, because the paper defers to WoBERT/BERT without restating them. The FFN, the norms and the head are therefore omitted from block_ops. context_length 1536 is the longest pre-training stage; stage 1 and the main downstream setting use 512, and a 1024 cut-off is also evaluated. The paper writes theta both as 10000^{-2(i-1)/d} and as 10000^{-2i/d}."
  },
